+# Integrations: Arize & Fiddler (Model Observability)
+
+This directory contains minimal scaffolding to integrate Arize and Fiddler for model observability.
+
+How to use:
+- Configure credentials via environment variables (ARIZE_API_KEY, FIDDLER_API_KEY, etc.)
+- From your model serving or adapter code, call:
+  - integrations.arize.arize_client.log_prediction(...)
+  - integrations.fiddler.fiddler_client.send_prediction_event(...)
+
+Recommended flow:
+1) At inference time, capture features, model outputs, model_version, request_id and trace_id.
+2) Emit a prediction event to Arize/Fiddler.
+3) When ground-truth becomes available, call log_label/send_label_event to record outcomes.
+
+Notes:
+- These are minimal HTTP clients. Replace with official SDKs for production where available.
+- Ensure PII is sanitized before sending to third-party services unless DPA/BYOK/private endpoints are in place.
