+# SOC2 Playbook (scaffold)
+
+This document outlines the typical steps and artifacts needed to achieve SOC2 readiness for Aegis.
+
+Controls & artifacts to prepare:
+- Access controls: RBAC configs, user & service account listing, MFA enforcement
+- Logging & monitoring: OTEL traces, log retention policy, alerting rules, SLOs
+- Change management: PR intake, CI/CD pipeline policies, deployment approvals
+- Vulnerability management: pentest reports, SAST/DAST pipeline outputs, remediation logs
+- Data protection: encryption at rest/in transit, key custody (HSM), BYOK evidence
+- Incident response: on-call runbooks, kill-switch exercise logs, incident timelines
+- Third-party management: DPA registers, vendor attestations, private endpoint configs
+
+Suggested workflow:
+1. Run SOC2 preflight (ci/compliance/soc2_preflight_check.sh)
+2. Collect the artifacts listed above and upload to MCP using attestation_collector.py
+3. Map artifacts to control IDs and assign control owners
+4. Engage auditor and provide the evidence package
+5. Track auditor findings and remediate, then re-submit evidence
+
